   $q$Paragraph 5 ends a mostly cause and effect passage with a solution. Why is this a fitting way to complete the structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The solution targets the cause named in paragraph 3, and the open beach shows the effect reversed.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The solution shows that algae will never again grow in Lake Morrow in any amount at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"The solution proves that the scientists in paragraph 3 named the wrong cause for the bloom.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The solution starts a new topic about native plants that has little to do with the bloom.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The solution targets the cause named in paragraph 3, and the open beach shows the effect reversed.$q$, $q$Using phosphorus-free fertilizer and planting grasses that soak up rainwater attack the fertilizer runoff from paragraph 3, and the beach staying open shows the problem easing. The passage says algae are always present in lakes, so it never claims they are gone forever.$q$, 'draft', 'a3d92be0-ae39-517d-9c45-827d5f737deb')
